// Examine text, one desc= per npc, keyed by 647 name through its id.
//
// Generated by tools/gen_examines_647.py -- do not edit desc= by hand;
// regenerate instead (a section's other keys are kept). 647's cache carries no
// examine text (it was server data by 2011), so it comes from, in order:
// void-634 (rev 634; no source found for its date) `examine` by npc id, then
// majula-289 (2005) `desc` by the same id. Ids are not all stable across that
// span (289's npc 297 is General Wartface, 647's a Guard; void-634's 553 is
// Aubury, 647's a banker), so a desc taken by id can be another npc's; where
// the two disagree, void-634's text is the one shown. A npc another file
// already defines has its desc in that file's section instead. Grade D:
// reference data, not checked against the live 2011 game text.
desc=She looks happy.

